         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--6. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE0_P0_RXPBDLYTG1_R4_RXPBDLYTG1_R4 ,Read DQ per-bit BDL delay (Timing Group 1). Trained to deskew the read DQ data that will be sampled by the incoming per-nibble read DQS, to improve the composite eye.  Bits 5-0 convey the BDL delay value. Bit 6 is Reserved.  The unit of change is a LSB in the control of the delay circuit, and is not denoninated in units of UI.  - Register Block Offset Address 0x069 controls the lane0 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x169 controls the lane1 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x269 controls the lane2 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x369 controls the lane3 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x469 controls the lane4 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x569 controls the lane5 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x669 controls the lane6 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x769 controls the lane7 read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x869 controls the lane[DBI] read deskew timing. (For Timing Group 1)  Note: This register is not per-pstate. The same deskew (for channel-routing differences) is used for all pstates.  Note: Timing Group 1 = RANK1. RESET:0x0"
          
