    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXDQSDLYTG3_U0_P2, Write DQS Delay (Timing Group DEST=3). RESET:0x100"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--9. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXDQSDLYTG3_U0_P2_TXDQSDLYTG3_U0_P2 ,Write DQS Delay (Timing Group DEST=3). Trained to set the delay from the memory-write command to the signal driving the write DQS  - Tx DQS Delay ( 10 bits, includes coarse and fine delays); (For Timing Group 3)  - TxDqsDlyTg3[9:6] is the coarse delay, ie one unit of delay is 1 UI.  - TxDqsDlyTg3[4:0] is the fine delay, ie one unit of delay is one-thirtysecond of a UI = UI/32.  - TxDqsDlyTg3[5] is reserved. Note: This register is per nibble, per timing-group, per pstate.  - Register Block Offset Address 0x0D3 controls the lower DQ nibble write DQS timing. (For Timing Group 3)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x1D3 controls the upper DQ nibble write DQS timing. (For Timing Group 3)  Note: Timing Group 3 = RANK3. RESET:0x100"
          
group.long  0x282++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL0_B1_P2, - Tx DQ driver impedance when equalization is enabled per nibble. - Register Block Offset Address 0x041 controls the lower DQ nibble - Register Block Offset Address 0x141 controls the upper DQ nibble RESET:0xfff"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--5. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL0_B1_P2_DRVSTRENDQP ,Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options. The 6-bit bus is used to select the target pull-down output impedance. Connects to the DrvStren pins of the driver thus:  - [Csr_DrvStren120P[2:0], Csr_DrvStren240P[1:0],Csr_DrvStren480P[0:0]] = [csrDrvStrenDqP]  - 000000 - HiZ.  - 000001 - 480.0  - 000010 - 240.0  - 000011 - 160.0  - 001000 - 120.0  - 001001 - 96.0  - 001010 - 80.0  - 001011 - 68.6  - 011000 - 60.0  - 011001 - 53.3  - 011010 - 48.0  - 011011 - 43.6  - 111000 - 40.0  - 111001 - 36.9  - 111010 - 34.3  - 111011 - 32.0  - 111110 - 30.0  - 111111 - 28.2 RESET:0x3f"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 6.--11. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL0_B1_P2_DRVSTRENDQN ,Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options. This 6-bit bus is used to select the target pull-down output impedance. Connects to the DrvStren pins of the driver thus:  [Csr_DrvStren120N[2:0],Csr_DrvStren240N[1:0],Csr_DrvStren480N[0:0]] = [csrDrvStrenDqN]  Note:See table of csr DrvStrenDqP for list of possible impedances. RESET:0x3f"
          
group.long  0x286++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_DQDQSRCVCNTRL_B1_P2, Connected to the rxdqs and rxdq Mode selects and trim controls, per nibble.  - Register Block Offset Address 0x043 controls the lower DQ nibble  - Register Block Offset Address 0x143 controls the upper DQ nibble This DFE feature may be used with MajorModeDbyte=011 only. RESET:0x5b0"
         bitfld.long 0x00 0. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_DQDQSRCVCNTRL_B1_P2_SELANALOGVREF ,Setting this signal high will force the local per-bit VREF generator to pass the global VREFA to the samplers. RESET:0x0"
          
         bitfld.long 0x00 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_DQDQSRCVCNTRL_B1_P2_EXTVREFRANGE ,Extends the range available in the local per-bit VREF generator. RESET:0x0"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 2.--3. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_DQDQSRCVCNTRL_B1_P2_DFECTRL ,This field is programmable as follows  - 00 - DFE off  - 01 - DFE on  - 10 - Train DFE0 Amplifier  - 11 - Train DFE1 Amplifier These settings are determined by PHY Training FW and should not be overridden. RESET:0x0"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 4.--6. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_DQDQSRCVCNTRL_B1_P2_MAJORMODEDBYTE ,Selects the major mode of operation for the receiver. These settings are determined by PHY Configuration based on DRAM protocol  - 000 - Input signal is terminated/referenced to VDDQ/2 (or unterminated)  - 001 - reserved  - 010 - Input signal is terminated/referenced to VSSQ  - 011 - Input signal is terminated/referenced to VDDQ  - 100 - reserved  - 101 - reserved  - 110 - reserved  - 111 - reserved RESET:0x3"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 7.--11. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_DQDQSRCVCNTRL_B1_P2_GAINCURRADJ ,Adjust gain current of RX amplifier stage. It is recommended to use default values for this CSR. RESET:0xb"
          
          
group.long  0x292++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL1_B1_P2, Tx impedance of DQ driver cells when equalization is disabled. - Register Block Offset Address 0x049 controls the lower DQ nibble - Register Block Offset Address 0x149 controls the upper DQ nibble RESET:0xfff"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--5. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL1_B1_P2_DRVSTRENFSDQP ,Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options This 6-bit bus is used to select the target pull-up output impedance. Connects to the DrvStren pins of the driver thus:  - [Csr_DrvStrenFS120P[2:0], Csr_DrvStrenFS240P[1:0], Csr_DrvStrenFS480P[0]] = [csrFSDrvStrenDq]  - 000000 - HiZ.  - 000001 - 480.0  - 000010 - 240.0  - 000011 - 160.0  - 001000 - 120.0  - 001001 - 96.0  - 001010 - 80.0  - 001011 - 68.6  - 011000 - 60.0  - 011001 - 53.3  - 011010 - 48.0  - 011011 - 43.6  - 111000 - 40.0  - 111001 - 36.9  - 111010 - 34.3  - 111011 - 32.0  - 111110 - 30.0  - 111111 - 28.2 RESET:0x3f"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 6.--11. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL1_B1_P2_DRVSTRENFSDQN ,Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options. This 6-bit bus is used to select the target pull-down output impedance. Connects to the DrvStren pins of the driver thus:  [Csr_DrvStrenFS120N[2:0], Csr_DrvStrenFS240N[1:0], Csr_DrvStrenFS480N[0:0]] = [csrDrvStrenDqN]  Note: See table of csr DrvStrenFSDqP for list of possible impedances. RESET:0x3f"
          
group.long  0x296++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL2_B1_P2, Tx DQ driver opposition impedance when equalization is enabled. - Register Block Offset Address 0x04b controls the lower DQ nibble - Register Block Offset Address 0x14b controls the upper DQ nibble RESET:0x0"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--5. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL2_B1_P2_DRVSTRENEQHIDQP ,Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options This 6-bit bus is used to select the target pull-up output impedance used in equalization. Connects to the DrvStren pins of the driver thus:  - [Csr_DrvStrenEQHi120P[2:0], Csr_DrvStrenEQHi240P[1:0], Csr_DrvStrenEQHi480P[0]] = [csrDrvStrenEQHiDq] RESET:0x0"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 6.--11. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXIMPEDANCECTRL2_B1_P2_DRVSTRENEQLODQN ,Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options This 6-bit bus is used to select the target pull-down output impedance used in equalization. Connects to the DrvStren pins of the driver thus:  - [Csr_DrvStrenEQLo120N[2:0], Csr_DrvStrenEQLo240N[1:0], Csr_DrvStrenEQLo480P[0]] = [csrDrvStrenEQLoDq] RESET:0x0"
          
group.long  0x29a++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXODTDRVSTREN_B1_P2, Selects desired impedance value for Host ODT. Must be set by user before PHY initialization. Setting for each protocol: DDR3:  - OdtStrenP - non-zero value  - OdtStrenN - same as OdtStrenP LPDDR3:  - OdtStrenP - non-zero value  - OdtStrenN - high-impedance DDR4:  - OdtStrenP - non-zero value  - OdtStrenN - high-impedance LPDDR4:  - OdtStrenP - high-impedance  - OdtStrenN - non-zero value  - Register Block Offset Address 0x04d controls the lower DQ nibble  - Register Block Offset Address 0x14d controls the upper DQ nibble RESET:0x0"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--5. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXODTDRVSTREN_B1_P2_ODTSTRENP ,Selects the ODT pull-up impedance.  Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options  - [ODTStren120P[2:0], ODTStren240P[1:0],ODTStren480P[0:0]]  - 000_00_0 = High Impedance  - 000_00_1 = 480 ohms  - 000_01_0 = 240 ohms  - 000_01_1 = 160 ohms  - 001_00_0 = 120 ohms  - 001_00_1 = 96.0 ohms  - 001_01_0 = 80.0 ohms  - 001_01_1 = 68.6 ohms  - 011_00_0 = 60.0 ohms  - 011_00_1 = 53.3 ohms  - 011_01_0 = 48.0 ohms  - 011_01_1 = 43.6 ohms  - 111_00_0 = 40.0 ohms  - 111_00_1 = 36.9 ohms  - 111_01_0 = 34.3 ohms  - 111_01_1 = 32.0 ohms  - 111_11_0 = 30.0 ohms  - 111_11_1 = 28.2 ohms RESET:0x0"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 6.--11. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXODTDRVSTREN_B1_P2_ODTSTRENN ,Selects the ODT pull-down impedance.  Refer to Technology specific PHY DATABOOK for supported options  - [ODTStren120N[2:0], ODTStren240N[1:0],ODTStren480N[0:0]]  - 000_00_0 = High Impedance  - 000_00_1 = 480 ohms  - 000_01_0 = 240 ohms  - 000_01_1 = 160 ohms  - 001_00_0 = 120 ohms  - 001_00_1 = 96.0 ohms  - 001_01_0 = 80.0 ohms  - 001_01_1 = 68.6 ohms  - 011_00_0 = 60.0 ohms  - 011_00_1 = 53.3 ohms  - 011_01_0 = 48.0 ohms  - 011_01_1 = 43.6 ohms  - 111_00_0 = 40.0 ohms  - 111_00_1 = 36.9 ohms  - 111_01_0 = 34.3 ohms  - 111_01_1 = 32.0 ohms  - 111_11_0 = 30.0 ohms  - 111_11_1 = 28.2 ohms RESET:0x0"
          
group.long  0x2be++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXSLEWRATE_B1_P2, Controls slew rates of the DQ/DQS drivers per nibble. - Tx predriver cal trims driver timing to account for clock duty cycle variation. - Register Block Offset Address 0x05f is the TxSlewRate for the lower nibble. - Register Block Offset Address 0x15f is the TxSlewRate for the upper nibble. RESET:0x7ff"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--3. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXSLEWRATE_B1_P2_TXPREP ,This is the 4-bit binary trim for the driver pull-up slew rate. 4'b0000 has a slower slew rate than 4'b1111 RESET:0xf"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 4.--7. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXSLEWRATE_B1_P2_TXPREN ,4 bit binary trim for the driver pull-down slew rate. 4'b0000 has a slower slew rate than 4'b1111 RESET:0xf"
          
         hexmask.long 0x00 8.--10. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_TXSLEWRATE_B1_P2_TXPREDRVMODE ,Controls predrivers to adjust timing of turn-on and turn-off of pull-up and pull-down segments. Recommended settings:  - DDR3 = 3'b011.  - DDR4 = 3'b010.  - LPDDR3 = 3'b010.  - LPDDR4 = 3'b001 RESET:0x7"
          
group.long  0x300++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_RXENDLYTG0_U1_P2, Trained Receive Enable Delay. (For Timing Group 0) RESET:0x100"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--10. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_RXENDLYTG0_U1_P2_RXENDLYTG0_U1_P2 ,Trained Receive Enable Delay. (For Timing Group 0) Trained to set the delay from the memory-read command to the signal enabling the read DQS to generate read-data strobes. The trained read DQS enable asserts during the read DQS preamble and deasserts at the end of the read burst.  - RxEnDlyTg0[10:6] is the coarse delay, ie one unit of delay is 1 UI.  - RxEnDlyTg0[4:0] is the fine delay, ie one unit of delay is one-thirtysecond of a UI = UI/32.  - RxEnDlyTg0[5] is reserved.  - Register Block Offset Address 0x080 controls the lower DQ nibble DqsEn. (For Timing Group 0)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x180 controls the upper DQ nibble DqsEn. (For Timing Group 0) Note: These Registers are replicated per pstate.  Note: Timing Group 0 = RANK0. RESET:0x100"
          
group.long  0x302++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_RXENDLYTG1_U1_P2, Trained Receive Enable Delay. (For Timing Group 1) RESET:0x100"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--10. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_DBYTE1_P2_RXENDLYTG1_U1_P2_RXENDLYTG1_U1_P2 ,Trained Receive Enable Delay. (For Timing Group 1) Trained to set the delay from the memory-read command to the signal enabling the read DQS to generate read-data strobes. The trained read DQS enable asserts during the read DQS preamble and deasserts at the end of the read burst.  - RxEnDlyTg1[10:6] is the coarse delay, ie one unit of delay is 1 UI.  - RxEnDlyTg1[4:0] is the fine delay, ie one unit of delay is one-thirtysecond of a UI = UI/32.  - RxEnDlyTg1[5] is reserved.  - Register Block Offset Address 0x081 controls the lower DQ nibble DqsEn. (For Timing Group 1)  - Register Block Offset Address 0x181 controls the upper DQ nibble DqsEn. (For Timing Group 1) Note: These Registers are replicated per pstate.  Note: Timing Group 1 = RANK1. RESET:0x100"
          
