tree "LPDDR4_PUB__DWC_DDRPHYA_ANIB0_P3"
base e:0x42600000
width 80.
group.long  0x100++0x3
    line.long 0x00 "LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_ANIB0_P3_ATXDLY_P3, Address/Command Delay, per pstate. RESET:0x0"
         hexmask.long 0x00 0.--6. 1. " LPDDR4_PUB_DWC_DDRPHYA_ANIB0_P3_ATXDLY_P3_ATXDLY_P3 ,Trained for LPDDR3/4 to generate timed address and command signals to the DRAMs, per ACX4. For DDR3/DDR4, it is recommended that address and command ACX4 have it ATxDly=0x00 The four signals generated by an ACX4 will have common timing.  - ATxDly[6] is the coarse delay, ie one unit of delay is 1 UI.  - ATxDly[5] is reserved.  - ATxDly[4:0] is the fine delay, ie one unit of delay is one-thirtysecond of a UI = UI/32. The target ACX4 used for memory clock generation, must have its ATxDly configured to 0x00. RESET:0x0"
          
tree.end

